sdiv6: x / 6, for x from -999 to 999, truncated toward zero. Inline: no call.
Listed at cells 10-26, with x in cell 90.
Copy cells 10-26 to where the program needs x / 6, with each 90 changed to the program's cell for x; the program goes on with x / 6 in the accumulator.
It overwrites the accumulator; x is kept.
Size 17 cells. It runs 17 instructions, straight through.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 10     190      CLA 90   cells 10-23: -333x / 1000 by Horner's rule (digits -3, -3, -3)
 11     790      SUB 90
 12     790      SUB 90
 13     790      SUB 90
 14     790      SUB 90
 15     401      SFT 01
 16     790      SUB 90
 17     790      SUB 90
 18     790      SUB 90
 19     401      SFT 01
 20     790      SUB 90
 21     790      SUB 90
 22     790      SUB 90
 23     401      SFT 01
 24     290      ADD 90   cells 24-26: plus 2x and a last shift: 1667x / 10^4, the truncations cancelling
 25     290      ADD 90
 26     401      SFT 01
 90     000      data: x, the program's cell, which is kept
